A sick eight-week-old puppy was the inspiring force behind a project to keep WA animal shelters on their feet.
The Sheltered Project has collated almost 200 images of animals in need of homes and the volunteers who look after them – an initiative that could raise tens of thousands of dollars.
Photo gallery Sheltered Project shines light on WA animal refuges
Project founder Michael Prendiville said he'd formed a soft spot for animals in need when his own dog became ill.
"When I first got my dog Jeffie when she was eight or nine weeks old she got really sick [from] an intestinal abnormality," he said.
"I was surprised because when you see them so down-and-out you're so surprised about how much of a bond you get with them and how much you'd do anything to make sure nothing bad happens to them.
"From that point on they became a real interest of mine."
